# Date Handling

`new Date('YYYY-MM-DD')` is UTC midnight and can shift the calendar day in western timezones when formatted locally.

Prefer helpers from `@/lib/common/date`:

```typescript
import { formatDateOnly, formatDateTime, parseDateLocal, toDateInputValue } from "@/lib/common/date";

formatDateOnly(row.startDate);           // table cells (date-only, UTC)
formatDateTime(row.expires);             // datetimes
toDateInputValue(row.startDate);         // <input type="date">
parseDateLocal(e.target.value);          // write local calendar date into store
```

```typescript
// ❌ May show previous day
new Date("2025-05-11").toLocaleDateString("en-US");

// ✅
formatDateOnly("2025-05-11");
```

Use UTC (`formatDateOnly`) for date-only DB values. Use `parseDateLocal` when the user picked a local calendar date in a form.
